@startuml ISO16757_Import_Workflow
title ISO16757 CSV import workflow (per-row revisions)

actor User
participant "Import UI / Admin View\n(properties/admin.py)" as AdminView
participant "Import Endpoint / view\n(properties/views.py)" as ImportView
participant "ISO16757 Import Service\n(properties/iso16757_import.py)" as ImportSvc
participant "Mapping Loader\n(properties/iso16757_mapping.py)" as Mapping
participant "django-reversion" as Reversion
participant "Audit signals\n(audit/signals.py)" as Audit
database "DB\n(properties/models.py + reversion versions)" as DB

User -> AdminView : Upload CSV + pick dictionary
AdminView -> ImportView : POST file, dictionary_id, user
ImportView -> Mapping : load mapping (ISO16757_MAPPING_FILE)
ImportView -> ImportSvc : parse_and_import(fileobj, dictionary, user)

note right of ImportSvc
  parse_and_import:
  - read headers
  - read 2nd row (PA-tags) -> header->PA mapping
  - create csv.DictReader
end note

ImportSvc -> ImportSvc : process rows
loop per CSV row
  ImportSvc -> Mapping : map CSV columns -> model attrs / pa keys
  ImportSvc -> Reversion : with reversion.create_revision()
  activate Reversion
    Reversion -> ImportSvc : enter revision context
    ImportSvc -> DB : find existing Property (by pa_code/guid) or create
    ImportSvc -> DB : create/update related models (names, definitions, examples, descriptions)
    ImportSvc -> DB : assign dictionary, groups, links (replaced/replacing)
    ImportSvc -> DB : save property and related objects
    ImportSvc -> Reversion : reversion.set_user(user); reversion.set_comment("ISO16757 import row X")
    ImportSvc -> Audit : (signals triggered by save) -> Audit rows created
    Reversion -> DB : persist version (includes followed related objects)
  deactivate Reversion
end
ImportSvc -> ImportView : return stats (created/updated/errors)
ImportView -> AdminView : render results page (summary)
User <-- AdminView : import results (UI message / link)

note left: See\n[`propbench/properties/iso16757_import.py`](propbench/properties/iso16757_import.py)\n[`propbench/properties/iso16757_mapping.py`](propbench/properties/iso16757_mapping.py)\n[`propbench/audit/signals.py`](propbench/audit/signals.py)
@enduml